                            <comment id="15688718" author="wmz7year" created="Wed, 23 Nov 2016 03:05:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1263&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1263&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15729414" author="agura" created="Wed, 7 Dec 2016 18:03:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=wmz7year&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;wmz7year&quot;&gt;wmz7year&lt;/a&gt;. I&apos;ve looked at your PR and I think that this fix isn&apos;t correct. Your cache can be created on some client or server node but this node can be filtered out and doesn&apos;t own any data. In order to get all nodes that really have cache data you should get affinity nodes using &lt;tt&gt;ClusterGroup.forDataNodes(String cacheName)&lt;/tt&gt; method.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also I&apos;m not sure that filtering out clients is good idea (&lt;tt&gt;forServers() call&lt;/tt&gt;) because client node can have local cache and own metrics.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Could you please take in account this comments and provide new fix?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
